// ADR 0059 c59_export_call: an `export "C"` C-ABI export, CALLED from Sentinel in
// the same file, so the fixture both builds-and-runs and enters every self-host
// STAGE differential (lex / ast / resolve / types / effects / borrow / mir /
// ctverify / codegen — each sweeps the FIXTURE corpus, `tests/pass` + `tests/ui`,
// alongside the real-program corpus, `examples/` + `sentinel_library/` + `tools/`).
// NOT `selfhost_merge`, which exercises only the compiler's own sources: the merge
// side of `export` is deliberately still unmirrored, see below.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS: `export` had no fixture at all, and that gap made the self-hosted
// parser's `export` handling structurally untestable. It hid a real defect —
// `dump_item` had an `extern` arm but no `export` one, so `export` fell through to
// `dump_fn_decl`, which read the ABI string as the fn NAME and mis-sliced the
// parameter list (`(fn "C" ((param ct_choose cond) …)`). Exactly the shape the
// `extern` arm was added to fix, and invisible for exactly the same reason. The
// real-program differential (examples/export/*) found it; this fixture pins it in
// the corpus so it cannot come back.
//
// WHAT IS STILL DEFERRED (ADR 0059): the export FEATURE mirror in `scg` — the
// `--lib` / `--emit-header` / shared-object modes, the multi-module symbol
// policy, and the whole MERGE side (neither `selfhost/merge/emit.sentinel`'s
// `emit_item` nor `selfhost/merge/engine.sentinel`'s `build_rename` has an
// `export` arm; the note on the new arm in `selfhost/parser/dump.sentinel` says
// why mirroring them NOW would break merge parity rather than restore it).
//
// This fixture stays inside the case `scg` does reproduce, and the discriminator
// is the ABI SHAPE, not the module count: an export whose parameters and return
// are the public value ABI (`i64` / `f64`) emits exactly the symbol an ordinary
// fn of the same name would (`@c59_ct_choose`), so `scg` matches the oracle by
// treating it as an ordinary fn. Be precise about WHY, per stage: the new
// `dump_item` arm buys `snc ast` parity and nothing else — `scg`'s COMPILE path
// never calls `dump_item`, and reaches the same place by a different route (its
// merge swallows `export` and the ABI string through the unknown-token
// fallthrough, so codegen only ever sees an ordinary fn). Reverting the arm
// leaves this fixture's `.ll` byte-identical and reddens only the ast
// differential. An export with a `&[u8]` parameter or a `[u8]` return does NOT
// (`export_needs_c_wrapper`, crates/sentinel-codegen): the body moves to
// `<name>__sentinel_impl` and the bare symbol becomes a generated C wrapper — in
// a single-file build too. `scg` does not model that, and no fixture covers it.
//
// The exported body is the ADR 0059 headline: a branch-free constant-time select
// over `secret` values behind a plain public `i64` API. c59_ct_choose(1, 42, 7) = 42.
//
// The symbol carries the `c59_` fixture prefix DELIBERATELY: an export emits a
// bare external-linkage C symbol, and this fixture is linked against the runtime
// staticlib, so a name under the runtime's reserved `sentinel_` prefix would be a
// duplicate-symbol hazard the day a runtime slice claims it (the ABI has grown
// 40 -> 51 symbols across the ADR 0071 slices alone), and the failure would name
// the runtime link rather than this fixture.

export "C" fn c59_ct_choose(cond: i64, a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
    let mask: secret i64 = 0 - cond;
    let notmask: secret i64 = mask ^ (0 - 1);
    let sa: secret i64 = a;
    let sb: secret i64 = b;
    declassify((sa & mask) | (sb & notmask))
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    c59_ct_choose(1, 42, 7)
}
